  <h2>Tips for your first Vipassana session</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Arrive a little early</strong> so you can settle in rather than rush in.</li>
    <li><strong>Wear modest, loose clothing.</strong> White or light colours are best at temples.</li>
    <li><strong>Use the cushion or chair that lets you sit comfortably.</strong> Good posture matters more than a perfect lotus position.</li>
    <li><strong>Expect a busy mind.</strong> Noticing that you got lost in thought <em>is</em> the practice, not a failure.</li>
    <li><strong>Keep going for 10 minutes a day afterwards.</strong> A short daily practice does more than one long session.</li>
  </ol>

  <p>Wondering whether you'd prefer full silence? Read <a href="/blog/silent-meditation-retreat-chiang-mai">Silent meditation retreats in Chiang Mai: what to expect</a>.</p>
